# ====================================================================
# twyne-cli env template
# ====================================================================
# `twyne tx` commands sign transactions. The signing key is Tier-1 per
# twyne-root CLAUDE.md §2.25 — it MUST come from a keystore at runtime.
# Operator walkthrough: docs/secrets-framework-guide.md (in twyne-root).
#
# Recommended for tx-signing flows:
#   op run --env-file=secrets/twyne-cli.env -- twyne tx ...
# where secrets/twyne-cli.env contains
#   PRIVATE_KEY=op://Twyne/twyne-cli/eoa-private-key
#   RPC_URL=op://Twyne/rpc/mainnet-keyed
#
# For read-only `twyne vault info` etc., a bare public RPC is fine:
#   RPC_URL=https://eth.drpc.org   (Tier-3 — public, no key)
# ====================================================================

# Tier-2 — RPC URL may embed a provider key. Bare public endpoints are
# Tier-3 (rate-limited but no credential). Source keyed endpoints from
# keystore in production:
#   RPC_URL=op://Twyne/rpc/mainnet-keyed
RPC_URL=https://eth.drpc.org

# Tier-1 — fund-bearing key. KEEP BLANK in this file.
# Source from keystore at runtime:
#   PRIVATE_KEY=op://Twyne/twyne-cli/eoa-private-key   (in secrets/twyne-cli.env)
# Plaintext fallback (NOT RECOMMENDED):
# PRIVATE_KEY=
